---
title: Sourdough country loaf
servings: 16
yield: 2 loaves
tags: [vegan, weekend]
time: 5 hours 35 minutes
source: Naturally Leavened Sourdough Bread by Susan Miller, King Arthur Baking, https://www.kingarthurbaking.com/recipes/naturally-leavened-sourdough-bread-recipe
---

> Make and feed the starter from Sourdough starter (baking/breads/sourdough).
> It should be ripe: fed, bubbly and risen.

In a #large bowl{}, mix 454 g (2 cups) of ripe sourdough starter with the @all-purpose flour{600%g}(or bread flour), @whole wheat flour{85%g} and @water{397%g}(room temperature) into a shaggy mass. Add a little water or flour if needed to get a soft, tacky dough.

Cover and rest ~{20%minutes}.

Add the @table salt{15%g} and knead until smooth and supple but still a little tacky. Cover and leave ~{1%hour}.

Turn the dough out, fold it in thirds like a letter, turn it 90 degrees, flatten it a little and fold in thirds again. Put it back in the bowl, cover and leave ~{1%hour} more.

Divide it in half and shape each piece into a loose round. Cover and rest ~{20%minutes}.

Shape each into a tight round or a bâtard and set it seam up in a floured #banneton{}, or a bowl lined with a floured cloth. Cover and leave ~{2%hours} to 2 1/2 hours, until light and airy.

About an hour before baking, heat the oven to 450°F (230°C) with a #baking stone{} in it and an empty #cast-iron frying pan{} on the rack below.

Turn the loaves out onto parchment, slash the tops and slide them, parchment and all, onto the stone. Pour 1 cup boiling water into the hot frying pan and shut the door.

Bake ~{35%minutes} to 40 minutes, until crusty and golden. Cool on a #wire rack{} before slicing.

> No stone: bake one loaf at a time in a #Dutch oven{} heated in the oven for
> 30 minutes, 20 minutes covered and 10 to 15 minutes uncovered.
